## Fixed this session: the previous version wrote the literal '"last_time":
## ' text before evaluating $lastStrikeTs -- Cheetah does not buffer or
## roll back literal output already written when a #try body's expression
## throws (int(None * 1000) throws TypeError when the station has never
## recorded lightning), so on failure the output was
## '"last_time": "last_time": null,' -- a duplicated key, invalid JSON.
## Same bug class as the one found and fixed in charts_json.tmpl this
## session. Fixed the same way: compute the raw value into a #set
## variable first (#set never emits literal output for a failing RHS),
## then emit the literal "key": value lines unconditionally afterward --
## reusing safeMs (already used throughout this file for exactly this
## raw-timestamp-or-null conversion) for last_time, and an inline
## ternary (fully evaluated before any output is written, so it can't
